      "**D.** → False\n\nThis statement claims $B\\setminus A=A\\setminus B$. Here $A\\setminus B=\\{a,b\\}$ collects $A$'s private letters while $B\\setminus A=\\{e\\}$ collects $B$'s private letter, and these two results have nothing in common. Since set subtraction runs in one direction only and gives different answers depending on which set is subtracted from which, the two differences are not equal, and the statement is false.",
