    solution_overview:
      "This problem sets up a universal set $U=\\{1,2,\\ldots,12\\}$, twelve consecutive integers, together with two subsets: $A=\\{1,3,5,7,9,11\\}$, explicitly the odd numbers among them, and $B=\\{2,4,6,8,10,12\\}$, explicitly the even numbers among them.\n\nThe key structural fact hiding inside these two definitions is that **every** whole number is odd or even, and **no** whole number is both at once. That fact about parity, combined with the explicit lists, determines everything else in the problem.\n\n**No overlap.** Since no number can be simultaneously odd and even, $A$ and $B$ share no element at all: $A\\cap B=\\emptyset$.\n\n**No gaps.** Since every one of the twelve numbers in $U$ is either odd (hence in $A$) or even (hence in $B$), the two sets together cover the whole universe: $A\\cup B=U=\\{1,2,\\ldots,12\\}$.\n\n**The complements.** Complementing $A$ means asking which numbers of $U$ are *not* odd, and the numbers that are not odd are precisely the even ones, so $A^c=\\{2,4,6,8,10,12\\}$, which is exactly the set $B$. By the same reasoning in reverse, $B^c=\\{1,3,5,7,9,11\\}$, which is exactly the set $A$.\n\n**Complementing the union.** Since $A\\cup B$ already equals the whole universe $U$, removing it from $U$ leaves nothing: $(A\\cup B)^c=U^c=\\emptyset$.\n\n**Complementing the intersection.** Since $A\\cap B$ is already empty, there is nothing to remove from the universe, so $(A\\cap B)^c=\\emptyset^c=U=\\{1,2,\\ldots,12\\}$.\n\n**Checking De Morgan's laws in this extreme case.** De Morgan's first law, $(A\\cup B)^c=A^c\\cap B^c$, becomes $A^c\\cap B^c=B\\cap A=\\emptyset$ (since $A^c=B$ and $B^c=A$), matching the $\\emptyset$ found directly above. De Morgan's second law, $(A\\cap B)^c=A^c\\cup B^c$, becomes $A^c\\cup B^c=B\\cup A=U$, matching the $U$ found directly above. Both identities hold, even in this special case where the two sets exactly partition the universe.\n\nWith $A\\cap B=\\emptyset$, $A\\cup B=U$, $A^c=B$, $B^c=A$, $(A\\cup B)^c=\\emptyset$, and $(A\\cap B)^c=U$ all pinned down, every one of the five statements can now be verified directly.",
