      "**A.** → True\n\nThis statement claims Dan is guilty. Clue (3) states this outright as a flat assertion, “Dan is guilty,” with no if-then structure and no further reasoning required to read it. Since clue (3) is given as a fact rather than a conditional rule, it settles the matter immediately on its own, so **Dan is guilty.**",
