      '**C.** → False\n\nThis statement claims that an evening where neither Owen nor Priya cooks, and Quinn cooks alone, is possible. Rule (2) requires at least one of Owen or Priya to cook on any valid night, and "Quinn alone" has neither of them present, so rule (2) is violated outright; Quinn is never given a role that lets her substitute for Owen or Priya in satisfying this requirement. **The statement is false.**',
