      '**A.** → False\n\nThis statement claims some valid scenario has Diego attending. The overview shows this is impossible: assuming Diego goes triggers rule (1) (Fatima goes), then rule (3) (Fatima\'s presence pushes Grace out), then rule (2) (with Grace out, Hugo must go to satisfy "Grace or Hugo"), then rule (6) (Hugo going forces Fatima out). This last step directly contradicts the Fatima going produced by rule (1) at the very start of the chain, so the assumption collapses under its own weight. Since assuming Diego attends leads to a contradiction using only rules (1), (3), (2), and (6), Diego cannot attend in any valid scenario at all. **The statement is false.**',
